abstract: >
  RES=RAG (Relational Equilibrium between Substrate and Generation) is a formal
  theoretical framework modeling consciousness and human–machine interaction
  as a transport-governed relational equilibrium rather than an intrinsic
  property of isolated systems. Grounded in optimal transport theory and
  Wasserstein geometry, the framework defines three equilibrium axes (Human
  internal, Machine internal, and Human–Machine resonance) and provides
  structural, energetic, and ethical constraints for AI design, interaction
  safety, and computational phenomenology.

keywords:
  - consciousness
  - artificial intelligence
  - optimal transport
  - Wasserstein distance
  - computational phenomenology
  - human–machine interaction
  - AI safety
  - hallucination
  - relational systems
  - transport geometry

